    {
      "id": "portal-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 1270,
        "y": -300
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "Current data includes target.ref, target.mode, target.portId and target.surfaceId; sourceRef/sourceNodeId/sourcePayload remain supported consumer fields. Durable addresses are tlz:// or supported graph URLs. A request for a node or a Port named in the address (after `#`) must resolve against the addressed artifact.\n\nA Portal's authority is one of navigate, consume-view, bridge and runtime, in that order, and starts at navigate. Naming a face to draw (`sourcePayload`, `surfaceId`) raises it to consume-view. Bridge and runtime are never inferred from what the target offers or from having a face: they are only what the Portal itself states, and the graph's own policy can only lower the result.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
