    {
      "id": "portal-examples",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Examples",
      "position": {
        "x": 2110,
        "y": 200
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Examples",
        "body": "The Portal under Examples, Back to the primitives, is a real Portal node: click it and the list of every primitive opens.\n\nTry it:\n1. Switch to edit mode (the pencil).\n2. Press Add node and choose Portal. A card appears.\n3. Select it and press Edit, or double-click it. Give it the address of the graph it opens onto. Under the address the editor says what it opens. If the graph exposes Ports, choose one to open onto it; that is optional.\n4. Switch to browse mode. The Portal shows the face of what it opens. Hover over it and press Enter, or click it as the navigation scheme describes.\n5. The other graph opens. A Portal only takes you there: nothing from it comes into the graph you are in.\n6. A missing destination is reported, and no replacement is invented.\n\nNo example graph is linked from this page yet.\n\nOn the Root page, the Weekend Reading Group route is a Page Route that acts as a Portal: a click opens that graph.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592072635,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
